1
00:00:01,900 --> 00:00:06,900
Maintenance and cleaning of the laser, welder 1200 watts.

2
00:00:06,900 --> 00:00:09,900
Clean or replace the lens protector.

3
00:00:09,900 --> 00:00:12,900
If the laser power decreases and the welding spark weakens,

4
00:00:12,900 --> 00:00:16,900
the welding head's lens protector may get dirty or damaged.

5
00:00:16,900 --> 00:00:18,900
Clean or replace it as needed.

6
00:00:18,900 --> 00:00:24,900
Please clean or replace the lens protector in a dust-free or relatively clean environment.

7
00:00:24,900 --> 00:00:29,900
Before operations, clean the welding head with lint-free paper or lint-free cloth

8
00:00:29,900 --> 00:00:32,900
and wash your hands or wear lint-free gloves.

9
00:00:32,900 --> 00:00:36,900
Remove the cover on the top of the welding head.

10
00:00:36,900 --> 00:00:38,900
Remove the lens protector one.

11
00:00:38,900 --> 00:00:43,500
Check the lens protector.

12
00:00:43,500 --> 00:00:47,500
If the lens protector is dirty, use a cotton swab dipped with alcohol to clean it.

13
00:00:47,500 --> 00:00:50,500
Then install it back to the welding head.

14
00:00:50,500 --> 00:00:55,500
If the lens protector is burned or heavily dirty and uncleanable, it needs to be replaced.

15
00:00:55,500 --> 00:01:00,500
Keep your hands clean or wear lint-free gloves to remove the gasket and lens protector.

16
00:01:00,500 --> 00:01:07,010
Take out a new lens protector.

17
00:01:07,010 --> 00:01:13,420
Do not touch the glass with your fingers or other tools during replacement to prevent dirt.

18
00:01:13,420 --> 00:01:19,420
If the glass accidentally gets dirty or dusty, use a cotton swab to clean it.

19
00:01:19,420 --> 00:01:25,040
Remove the protective film on the top.

20
00:01:25,040 --> 00:01:27,040
Install the lens protector.

21
00:01:27,040 --> 00:01:30,040
Remove the protective film on the other side.

22
00:01:30,040 --> 00:01:32,040
Install the gasket back.

23
00:01:32,040 --> 00:01:44,000
Install the lens protector back to the welding head.

24
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:48,000
Install the lens protector in the correct direction and press it into place.

25
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:55,750
Calibrate the red spot position for the welding head.

26
00:01:55,750 --> 00:01:57,750
Calibrate the left or right offset.

27
00:01:57,750 --> 00:02:03,750
If you use the pre-installed welding nozzle for laser welding, perform a left or right offset calibration

28
00:02:03,750 --> 00:02:09,750
when the laser spot deviates left or right from the wire, despite proper nozzle installation.

29
00:02:09,750 --> 00:02:17,750
On the touchscreen of the main unit, tap system settings, machine settings, enter administrator settings.

30
00:02:17,750 --> 00:02:26,060
Then input the 8 digit password, 8888888.

31
00:02:26,060 --> 00:02:29,060
To the right of red spot position offset, tap start.

32
00:02:29,060 --> 00:02:34,060
Then tap the left arrow to decrease the offset and move the red spot leftward.

33
00:02:34,060 --> 00:02:38,060
Tap the right arrow to increase the offset and move the red spot rightward.

34
00:02:38,060 --> 00:02:42,060
When the center of the red spot falls at the welding wire, tap completed.

35
00:02:42,060 --> 00:02:44,060
Calibrate the up or down offset.

36
00:02:44,060 --> 00:02:52,060
When a cutting nozzle is used, the laser beam may strike the nozzle's inner wall, resulting in either blockage or reflection.

37
00:02:52,060 --> 00:02:58,230
In such cases, perform left or right offset calibration.

38
00:02:58,230 --> 00:03:08,080
If the problem persists, reset the red spot position offset to zero and try calibrating the up or down offset.

39
00:03:08,080 --> 00:03:13,080
Welding and cleaning nozzles have larger apertures and typically do not require such adjustment.

40
00:03:13,080 --> 00:03:20,080
Insert the hex key into hole 1 or hole 2 and slowly turn the screw while observing the light emitting from the nozzle.

41
00:03:20,080 --> 00:03:24,080
If a clear red spot appears, stop turning the screw.

42
00:03:24,080 --> 00:03:30,380
Replace the welding wire.

43
00:03:30,380 --> 00:03:35,380
Now we replace the 1 millimeter welding wire with a 1.2 millimeter welding wire.

44
00:03:35,380 --> 00:03:40,380
Open the door of the wire feeder, unscrew the cap and remove the sleeve.

45
00:03:41,380 --> 00:03:44,380
Open the two tensioners.

46
00:03:44,380 --> 00:03:50,380
Rotate the wire spool clockwise to remove the wire from the wire feeding driver.

47
00:03:50,380 --> 00:03:53,380
Take out the wire spool.

48
00:03:53,380 --> 00:03:57,380
Bend the wire end and store it in the hole of the wire spool.

49
00:03:57,380 --> 00:04:01,690
Remove the screws.

50
00:04:01,690 --> 00:04:03,690
Remove the current drive rolls.

51
00:04:03,690 --> 00:04:06,690
Remove the screws above the wire feeding driver.

52
00:04:06,690 --> 00:04:10,690
Take out the drive roll stored above the wire feeding driver.

53
00:04:10,690 --> 00:04:15,690
Ensure that the size on the outer side of the drive rolls matches the welding wires diameter.

54
00:04:15,690 --> 00:04:19,690
Install the new pair of drive rolls.

55
00:04:19,690 --> 00:04:22,690
Install the screws back.

56
00:04:22,690 --> 00:04:26,690
Store the other pair of drive rolls above the wire feeding driver.

57
00:04:26,690 --> 00:04:37,510
Replace the 0.8 slash 1.0 nozzle with the provided 1.2 slash 1.6 wire feeding nozzle.

58
00:04:37,510 --> 00:04:40,510
Install the new wire spool.

59
00:04:40,510 --> 00:04:42,510
Install the sleeve back.

60
00:04:42,510 --> 00:04:43,510
Install the cap back.

61
00:04:43,510 --> 00:04:47,300
Take out the wire end.

62
00:04:47,300 --> 00:04:50,300
Cut off the bent end of the wire.

63
00:04:50,300 --> 00:04:53,300
Thread the wire into the wire feeding driver.

64
00:04:53,300 --> 00:04:56,300
Press the wire slightly to make it pass through.

65
00:04:56,300 --> 00:05:04,100
Close the tensioners.

66
00:05:04,100 --> 00:05:10,300
Rotate the tensioners knobs to adjust the wire feed tension.

67
00:05:10,300 --> 00:05:15,300
Press and hold the feed button on the wire feeder until the wire extends out from the nozzle.

68
00:05:15,300 --> 00:05:18,300
Maintenance and cleaning of the CNC cutter.

69
00:05:18,300 --> 00:05:24,980
Clean the nozzle.

70
00:05:24,980 --> 00:05:27,980
The nozzle can be very hot after processing.

71
00:05:27,980 --> 00:05:30,980
Wear heat resistant gloves before you touch it.

72
00:05:30,980 --> 00:05:48,630
Clean the base plate.

73
00:05:48,630 --> 00:06:00,160
Clean the base plate with an alcohol dipped lint free cloth when necessary.

74
00:06:00,160 --> 00:06:11,120
Clean the camera lens.

75
00:06:11,120 --> 00:06:32,420
Clean the strip lights.

76
00:06:32,420 --> 00:06:49,740
Clean the protective lid.

77
00:06:49,740 --> 00:07:28,840
Clean the fixture and the dust proof plate.

78
00:07:28,840 --> 00:07:29,840
Clean the slats.

79
00:07:29,840 --> 00:08:36,220
Clean the exhaust fan.

80
00:08:36,220 --> 00:08:38,220
Disassemble the exhaust fan.

81
00:08:38,220 --> 00:10:59,100
Clean the exhaust fan.

82
00:10:59,100 --> 00:11:01,100
Clean the base plate slides.
